00:16:51,766 --> 00:16:54,328
In another case, the sub-inspector
who was investigating the case

257
00:16:54,353 --> 00:16:55,398
was smashed by a hammer

258
00:16:55,959 --> 00:16:58,461
and was brutally murdered
by being shot at close range.

259
00:16:59,816 --> 00:17:01,031
Are these two incidents connected?

260
00:17:01,116 --> 00:17:03,414
Who's behind all this?
We have no clue about it.

261
00:17:04,199 --> 00:17:06,625
We did not issue an official statement yet.

262
00:17:07,263 --> 00:17:10,226
If word gets out,
it'll tarnish our department's reputation.

263
00:17:10,833 --> 00:17:13,476
Find out who murdered the inspector.

264
00:17:14,377 --> 00:17:15,141
Be brutal!

265
00:17:20,662 --> 00:17:21,175
Yes, Sir!

266
00:17:22,195 --> 00:17:23,234
Four guys arrived at the spot.

267
00:17:23,692 --> 00:17:25,414
-They arrived in two vehicles.
-What kind of vehicles?

268
00:17:26,164 --> 00:17:27,314
An old Yamaha bike.

269
00:17:27,853 --> 00:17:30,555
Another one...
I believe it was blue, Suzuki.

270
00:17:30,824 --> 00:17:32,820
They were... wearing masks, Sir.

271
00:17:33,282 --> 00:17:36,336
One of the guys... had curly hair.

272
00:17:37,367 --> 00:17:38,391
It's that guy who shot him.

273
00:17:38,958 --> 00:17:40,508
The others were chasing me down.

274
00:17:42,666 --> 00:17:43,961
What kind of gun did he use?

275
00:17:44,902 --> 00:17:46,547
The type we see in movies a lot.

276
00:17:46,983 --> 00:17:49,797
Where they pop it out,
load bullets, and whirl it.

277
00:17:51,047 --> 00:17:53,008
The one that holds six bullets.

278
00:17:53,969 --> 00:17:54,648
What about the one who shot you?

279
00:17:55,297 --> 00:17:57,812
It's the kind where you pull to shoot.

280
00:17:58,525 --> 00:17:59,328
That kind of gun, Sir.

281
00:18:01,303 --> 00:18:02,828
Yeah, that's the one!

282
00:18:10,621 --> 00:18:11,422
You must stay put locally.

283
00:18:11,637 --> 00:18:13,101
-If we need you, we'd call you.
-Sure, Sir.

284
00:18:14,395 --> 00:18:18,057
" Malayla, Malayla "

285
00:18:19,956 --> 00:18:22,745
" My mama, my body’s low fire "

286
00:18:24,331 --> 00:18:28,174
" My mama, you’re slayin’
My trouble empire "

287
00:18:30,659 --> 00:18:33,147
" Malayla, Malayla, move it for me "

288
00:18:33,172 --> 00:18:35,492
" Malayla, Malayla, deeper you breathe "

289
00:18:35,634 --> 00:18:38,024
" Malayla, Malayla, know when you need "

290
00:18:38,109 --> 00:18:40,557
" Malayla, Malayla, dark energy "

291
00:18:40,582 --> 00:18:42,424
" Dark energy... Dark energy... "

292
00:18:42,588 --> 00:18:44,081
Brother, Arasu's men are here.

293
00:18:48,456 --> 00:18:49,698
Arasu filled me in.

294
00:18:50,788 --> 00:18:54,690
If you don't bring any trouble,
you could stay here.

295
00:18:55,168 --> 00:18:58,260
Until you stay here...

296
00:18:58,672 --> 00:19:00,346
you better shut up, your gob,
and stay put.

297
00:19:01,737 --> 00:19:02,549
Understand?

298
00:19:03,922 --> 00:19:05,497
-Mavattam.
-Yes, Brother.

299
00:19:06,437 --> 00:19:08,099
-Keep an eye on them.
-I'll handle them.

300
00:19:08,865 --> 00:19:09,661
Come with me.

301
00:19:30,849 --> 00:19:32,263
The toilet is on this side.

302
00:19:32,793 --> 00:19:34,529
If you need anything,
holler Mavattam.

303
00:19:35,213 --> 00:19:36,370
Remember what my Boss mentioned.

304
00:19:36,804 --> 00:19:38,240
Understood? I'm leaving.

305
00:19:39,568 --> 00:19:41,193
-Mavattam!
-What is it?

306
00:19:41,218 --> 00:19:43,130
-Just checking.
-Okay.

307
00:19:43,379 --> 00:19:46,280
Look, bury your pride and
arrogance for a few days.

308
00:19:46,607 --> 00:19:48,068
Even if someone spits on your face...

309
00:19:48,327 --> 00:19:49,982
wipe it off, say sorry, and keep walking.

310
00:19:50,323 --> 00:19:51,482
-Okay?
-Sure!

311
00:19:51,745 --> 00:19:52,944
This applies to everyone.

312
00:19:53,364 --> 00:19:54,966
Hey, where are you going?

313
00:19:56,209 --> 00:19:57,044
I heard you, Bud.

314
00:19:57,461 --> 00:19:59,161
Not to get angry
even if someone spits on you.

315
00:19:59,591 --> 00:20:00,554
I won't get angry.

316
00:20:00,877 --> 00:20:02,224
Karuppu, I'll rip your mouth out.

317
00:20:02,959 --> 00:20:04,271
-He did you dirty.
-Why do you have to go down to drink?

318
00:20:04,465 --> 00:20:06,576
-Hey, stop poking the bear.
-Hey, Das, I'm coming too.

319
00:20:14,316 --> 00:20:15,740
One out of two troublemakers is sloshed.

320
00:20:16,357 --> 00:20:17,638
I'll be happy if the other is sloshed too.

321
00:20:19,115 --> 00:20:19,622
Go easy on him!

322
00:20:20,152 --> 00:20:23,193
He's already upset
that his father is not talking to him.

323
00:20:40,327 --> 00:20:44,633
" Relationships, an endless tale "

324
00:20:44,793 --> 00:20:49,036
" Emotions, tales untold "

325
00:20:49,253 --> 00:20:53,419
" Some stories never end "

326
00:20:53,784 --> 00:20:58,075
" An ending
May still lead to another story "

327
00:20:58,283 --> 00:21:04,992
" May all that follows be joyful "

328
00:21:07,809 --> 00:21:11,668
" The burden your heart bears "

329
00:21:15,333 --> 00:21:20,617
Devadas, please don't dwell on
what your uncles did to us.

330
00:21:21,402 --> 00:21:24,635
Your focus should be entirely on education.

331
00:21:27,298 --> 00:21:29,969
Hey! Who the hell are you?

332
00:21:32,103 --> 00:21:34,680
-I don't care who the heck it is.
-Kitty, where is he going?

333
00:21:36,316 --> 00:21:37,795
If you're a man, face me!

334
00:21:43,751 --> 00:21:45,732
-Hey, who the hell are you?
-Here comes trouble!

335
00:22:01,382 --> 00:22:02,544
Until the song ends...

336
00:22:04,517 --> 00:22:06,968
[shushing]

337
00:22:11,777 --> 00:22:12,318
Hey, Das!

338
00:22:14,636 --> 00:22:16,029
Have you lost your mind?
Let's go!

339
00:22:21,915 --> 00:22:22,982
Hey, let's go!

340
00:22:24,063 --> 00:22:25,479
-Please continue singing.
-Hey!

341
00:22:27,383 --> 00:22:28,795
-You leave. I'll bring him.
-You're testing my patience.

342
00:22:28,904 --> 00:22:30,032
-You better bring him.
-Fine, you leave.

343
00:22:30,391 --> 00:22:32,391
-Freaking mess!
-Das? Das?

344
00:22:33,019 --> 00:22:35,177
We can listen to the song tomorrow.
Let's go from here.

345
00:22:37,141 --> 00:22:37,942
Please get up.

346
00:22:38,662 --> 00:22:39,188
Let's go!

347
00:22:40,114 --> 00:22:40,740
Careful!

348
00:22:42,416 --> 00:22:43,063
Keep walking.

349
00:22:43,228 --> 00:22:45,005
Sir, that's a very old case.

350
00:22:45,414 --> 00:22:46,818
You're saying it was 15 years ago.

351
00:22:47,221 --> 00:22:49,140
I cannot dig up files so far.
It's difficult, Sir.

352
00:22:50,364 --> 00:22:51,191
Sir?!

353
00:22:52,192 --> 00:22:53,512
Sir, someone might notice.

354
00:22:53,975 --> 00:22:56,172
-Please dig out the information.
-Just two minutes, Sir.

355
00:23:01,922 --> 00:23:02,922
-Sir, he's back.
-Sir.

356
00:23:06,339 --> 00:23:08,320
This is Arasu and his new team.

357
00:23:19,167 --> 00:23:20,505
He came out of nowhere!

358
00:23:21,534 --> 00:23:22,521
Gave him one tight slap!

359
00:23:22,887 --> 00:23:26,107
Despite warnings,
your guy caused a problem.

360
00:23:26,898 --> 00:23:29,505
Listen closely!
None of you should come downstairs.

361
00:23:29,905 --> 00:23:33,380
Is he emotional about the song,
or does he have feelings for you?

362
00:23:36,792 --> 00:23:37,919
They were high and acted in haste.

363
00:23:38,326 --> 00:23:38,943
I'll handle them.

364
00:23:40,492 --> 00:23:41,193
Fine, let's go.

365
00:23:44,025 --> 00:23:46,161
Fine, Solo and I are going to the movie.
Wanna join?

366
00:23:46,404 --> 00:23:48,177
No! I have to finish writing.
You guys carry on.

367
00:23:49,499 --> 00:23:51,747
If you keep isolating yourself,
you'll go crazy.

368
00:23:53,502 --> 00:23:54,927
-Sarah!
-Are you coming?

369
00:23:58,522 --> 00:23:59,880
I wonder when you'll finish writing.

370
00:24:08,850 --> 00:24:11,474
Why don't we go downstairs
to have a drink?

371
00:24:12,328 --> 00:24:13,458
No freaking way, Dude!

372
00:24:13,927 --> 00:24:14,833
Shut up and drink here.

373
00:24:15,838 --> 00:24:18,060
Hey, he wishes to listen to a song.

374
00:24:18,603 --> 00:24:19,677
Let him go. We'll manage it.

375
00:24:20,071 --> 00:24:22,499
Hey, he's calm about it.
Why are you fueling him?

376
00:24:22,841 --> 00:24:23,630
Are you his yes man?

377
00:24:24,467 --> 00:24:25,529
You're hard to talk to.

378
00:24:26,648 --> 00:24:28,615
Daily looking at the same faces

379
00:24:28,801 --> 00:24:30,643
seems like we're already in a prison.

380
00:24:31,145 --> 00:24:35,213
"O moon, don't come close to me "

381
00:24:35,890 --> 00:24:40,521
" I'm not where you imagine me to be "

382
00:24:40,894 --> 00:24:41,822
Hey, play your card.

383
00:24:42,236 --> 00:24:46,498
" O moon, don't come close to me "

384
00:24:46,947 --> 00:24:52,429
" I'm not where you imagine me to be "

385
00:24:53,293 --> 00:24:57,463
" O flower, don't be enchanted by me "

386
00:24:57,488 --> 00:24:59,021
-Hey, Das, where are you going?
-Dude, what happened?

387
00:24:59,088 --> 00:25:00,782
-Get me a full bottle.
-You ruined the game.

388
00:25:01,643 --> 00:25:04,056
" ...you imagine me to be "

389
00:25:04,255 --> 00:25:06,508
-" O moon, don't come close to me "
-Shut up!

390
00:25:15,237 --> 00:25:18,644
" ...me to be "

391
00:25:32,344 --> 00:25:32,953
Where is he going?

392
00:25:33,571 --> 00:25:34,781
Does he think we are all fools?

393
00:25:35,195 --> 00:25:38,001
Das, her magnetic voice
is drawing you out, is it?

394
00:25:38,121 --> 00:25:40,100
-Yeah, so what? Shut up and sit tight.
-Das!

395
00:25:40,185 --> 00:25:42,062
Das, you caused a problem yesterday.
Please get back inside.

396
00:25:43,125 --> 00:25:44,469
Let him go. He won't go far.

397
00:25:44,576 --> 00:25:45,022
Hey!

398
00:25:45,469 --> 00:25:47,656
Hey, If he causes trouble,
I'll slit your throat.

399
00:25:48,211 --> 00:25:50,969
Let him go.
Always controlling everyone.

400
00:26:08,338 --> 00:26:09,380
Are you looking for someone?

401
00:26:17,098 --> 00:26:18,331
Are you short-tempered?

402
00:26:19,331 --> 00:26:20,294
I saw you fighting yesterday.

403
00:26:20,319 --> 00:26:23,449
Erm... that was my most favorite song.

404
00:26:24,058 --> 00:26:27,162
After my mother's demise,
Dad used to play this song so often.

405
00:26:28,451 --> 00:26:30,617
Moreover, that guy was interrupting
by talking over the phone.

406
00:26:31,316 --> 00:26:31,873
So, I did it!

407
00:26:32,083 --> 00:26:33,726
How long has it been
since your mother died?

408
00:26:35,247 --> 00:26:37,398
Must be around 15-16 years.

409
00:26:40,670 --> 00:26:42,525
Are you living here?

410
00:26:43,420 --> 00:26:44,307
For a month now.

411
00:26:45,896 --> 00:26:46,746
After that?

412
00:26:47,833 --> 00:26:50,225
After that,
a new town and a new hotel.

413
00:26:50,801 --> 00:26:51,600
And a different crowd.

414
00:26:52,333 --> 00:26:53,254
But songs remain the same.

415
00:26:54,497 --> 00:26:55,154
What about your family?

416
00:26:59,902 --> 00:27:00,775
Why are you laughing?

417
00:27:01,834 --> 00:27:04,461
Are you wondering why you would
share anything with a stranger?

418
00:27:05,580 --> 00:27:08,113
You hesitate to tell the truth
to those you know.

419
00:27:08,366 --> 00:27:09,925
But you can pour your heart out
to a stranger.

420
00:27:11,501 --> 00:27:13,349
You're right!
I don't have to pretend.

421
00:27:15,013 --> 00:27:16,453
So, tell me, stranger.
What about you?

422
00:27:16,933 --> 00:27:17,630
I...

423
00:27:18,929 --> 00:27:19,962
What happened, stranger?

424
00:27:22,803 --> 00:27:24,442
Telling the truth is difficult.

425
00:27:34,529 --> 00:27:37,719
You do what you love.
So, it's easy for you to share.

426
00:27:39,241 --> 00:27:41,219
I'm doing something I don't love.

427
00:27:41,897 --> 00:27:43,123
So, it's a bit difficult to share.

428
00:27:45,225 --> 00:27:47,960
What makes you say
that I do what I love?

429
00:27:49,315 --> 00:27:51,743
You smoke, you sing,
and you are having fun.

430
00:27:52,274 --> 00:27:53,567
Why would you do it
if you don't love it?

431
00:27:59,823 --> 00:28:01,268
This is a guise I wear to earn a living.

432
00:28:05,394 --> 00:28:06,315
So, what do you love to do?

433
00:28:13,104 --> 00:28:14,071
Nothing much, though.

434
00:28:14,687 --> 00:28:16,880
I had a small desire.
Now even that has faded away.

435
00:28:19,193 --> 00:28:20,833
Why? What happened to it?

436
00:28:30,526 --> 00:28:33,583
Whenever I sing at a hotel,
I start to wonder, looking at the crowd...

437
00:28:34,895 --> 00:28:36,193
One day without wearing this disguise...

438
00:28:37,357 --> 00:28:39,417
I wish to come as a guest
and enjoy listening to someone sing.

439
00:28:41,297 --> 00:28:42,997
That's it. Nothing else.

440
00:28:44,903 --> 00:28:47,872
Then come over tomorrow
and give me company.

441
00:28:48,894 --> 00:28:50,691
The braided girl did sing well.

442
00:28:50,910 --> 00:28:51,792
Let her take over.

443
00:28:57,302 --> 00:28:59,693
I'm serious about it.
Please join me tomorrow.

444
00:29:06,007 --> 00:29:07,633
No need.
It'll become an issue.

445
00:29:09,135 --> 00:29:10,490
Please hear me out.

446
00:29:11,067 --> 00:29:12,740
The owner of this place is known to me.

447
00:29:13,683 --> 00:29:16,553
You hang out with me tomorrow.
Take a day off.

448
00:29:17,030 --> 00:29:20,213
Hey, what are you doing for so long,
damn it?

449
00:29:21,369 --> 00:29:22,024
Get back!

450
00:29:26,260 --> 00:29:28,693
I don't know your name,
and you don't know mine.

451
00:29:29,010 --> 00:29:30,677
We will not get familiar.
And it's not required.

452
00:29:30,911 --> 00:29:32,884
What was that you said?
Ah... strangers!

453
00:29:33,750 --> 00:29:34,529
We'd stay strangers!

454
00:29:34,999 --> 00:29:36,232
But please hang out with me tomorrow.

455
00:29:39,552 --> 00:29:40,224
You are coming!

456
00:29:45,833 --> 00:29:48,193
Only a week is left
for the sister's wedding.

457
00:29:48,578 --> 00:29:50,286
We still haven't started
sending out invitations.

458
00:29:51,108 --> 00:29:51,872
Are you listening?

459
00:29:52,811 --> 00:29:54,811
I'm not able to
handle everything alone out here.

460
00:29:54,855 --> 00:29:57,224
Please handle it.
I have spoken to my senior.

461
00:29:57,289 --> 00:29:59,411
-I'll be there soon.
-Sir! Sir!

462
00:30:00,102 --> 00:30:02,802
Either fix your phone
or fix your family.

463
00:30:03,482 --> 00:30:05,224
Always on speakerphone
with annoying problems.

464
00:30:05,249 --> 00:30:06,724
If you don't make it,
people will talk.

465
00:30:07,323 --> 00:30:09,582
He is Arasu, an ex-police officer.

466
00:30:09,651 --> 00:30:12,986
15 years ago, for supplying
discarded guns to the naxals...

467
00:30:13,011 --> 00:30:14,328
he was arrested and locked up in prison.

468
00:30:14,844 --> 00:30:15,469
There he met...

469
00:30:16,703 --> 00:30:17,234
Das.

470
00:30:19,244 --> 00:30:20,031
Sebastian.

471
00:30:21,302 --> 00:30:22,273
Karuppan.

472
00:30:23,974 --> 00:30:24,656
Kitty.

473
00:30:25,673 --> 00:30:29,094
He formed a team with them
and escaped from the prison.

474
00:30:29,343 --> 00:30:31,291
And have been operating as a gang to date.

475
00:30:31,777 --> 00:30:33,206
How are they related to this case?

476
00:30:33,581 --> 00:30:36,258
We investigated an eyewitness in
the recent inspector's murder case.

477
00:30:36,845 --> 00:30:39,242
His description perfectly matches theirs.

478
00:30:40,358 --> 00:30:43,656
Keeping Arasu's history
and the current armed robbery in mind...

479
00:30:44,060 --> 00:30:45,248
followed by the inspector's murder,

480
00:30:45,341 --> 00:30:46,544
and eyewitness's statement.

481
00:30:46,904 --> 00:30:51,237
From all this, I have a hunch
that they're behind all of it.

482
00:30:52,506 --> 00:30:53,118
Okay.

483
00:30:53,769 --> 00:30:55,693
Quickly finish up the investigation
and update me.

484
00:30:55,869 --> 00:30:56,583
Thank you, Sir.

485
00:31:11,992 --> 00:31:13,187
Hey, shall we go?

486
00:31:14,573 --> 00:31:17,609
I have a slight headache.
Could you manage alone today?

487
00:31:18,417 --> 00:31:19,687
It doesn't look like you got a headache.

488
00:31:21,081 --> 00:31:23,859
Still, I believe you.
Fine, just for today.

489
00:31:24,162 --> 00:31:24,913
Take care!

490
00:31:44,050 --> 00:31:44,607
You came!

491
00:31:45,413 --> 00:31:46,544
I thought you weren't coming.

492
00:31:49,769 --> 00:31:51,935
Headache? I'll handle you later.

493
00:31:56,123 --> 00:31:58,060
Come on, relax!

494
00:32:01,216 --> 00:32:02,332
Would you like to have a drink?

495
00:32:03,466 --> 00:32:03,896
No.

496
00:32:06,459 --> 00:32:07,490
What are you doing over here?

497
00:32:08,152 --> 00:32:09,765
Hello, over here!

498
00:32:11,661 --> 00:32:12,458
One PSOP.

499
00:32:12,738 --> 00:32:14,122
I'm speaking to her, not you.

500
00:32:14,182 --> 00:32:14,872
Why not ask me?

501
00:32:17,044 --> 00:32:17,818
One PSOP.

502
00:32:18,263 --> 00:32:19,919
-And you?
-No...

503
00:32:20,917 --> 00:32:23,482
-Shall I make it two?
-No, apple juice.

504
00:32:25,824 --> 00:32:27,310
Hey, ice cubes.

505
00:32:31,067 --> 00:32:34,487
" Silent tunes find their voice "

506
00:32:34,519 --> 00:32:37,854
" Your breath lingers with mine "

507
00:32:37,956 --> 00:32:40,245
" Moonlight drizzles softly "

508
00:32:40,402 --> 00:32:41,917
I'm leaving!

509
00:32:45,084 --> 00:32:46,937
Hey, what is it?
Are you going to feed her?

510
00:32:48,032 --> 00:32:49,305
I'll call you if I need anything.

511
00:32:50,282 --> 00:32:51,200
Please sit down.

512
00:32:51,443 --> 00:32:54,180
