1499
01:38:02,110 --> 01:38:03,875
Hey, why are you talking about
irrelevant stuff?

1500
01:38:03,900 --> 01:38:05,383
First, answer why you shot him?

1501
01:38:07,133 --> 01:38:09,281
You killed him because he did bad things.

1502
01:38:10,226 --> 01:38:12,476
I killed him because he did bad things.

1503
01:38:15,349 --> 01:38:18,687
When I told you I had no more desire
to become a mother...

1504
01:38:19,756 --> 01:38:20,828
you asked me why.

1505
01:38:25,040 --> 01:38:28,219
He ripped out my uterus when I was 16

1506
01:38:28,805 --> 01:38:31,117
looked in my face, laughed, and said

1507
01:38:33,878 --> 01:38:36,750
"You can never become a mother
in your life."

1508
01:38:41,049 --> 01:38:42,414
It wasn't just me...

1509
01:38:44,150 --> 01:38:46,760
all the girls over there
went through the same tragedy.

1510
01:38:50,265 --> 01:38:51,370
That's why I killed him.

1511
01:38:58,108 --> 01:39:00,986
Please tell me if I'm becoming
a problem to you people...

1512
01:39:03,181 --> 01:39:04,409
I'll go away from here.

1513
01:39:24,840 --> 01:39:27,253
-Hey, Chunnilal, walk faster.
-Shut up and follow me.

1514
01:39:34,156 --> 01:39:35,057
Hurry up, guys!

1515
01:39:38,455 --> 01:39:40,463
-Hey, hand me that bag.
-What is it?

1516
01:39:41,409 --> 01:39:43,776
-Hand me the bag!
-Hey, why are you inviting trouble?

1517
01:39:44,223 --> 01:39:46,228
-Hey, guys, hurry up!
-Here you go!

1518
01:39:50,753 --> 01:39:52,040
You carry on. I'll be back.

1519
01:39:52,275 --> 01:39:53,643
-Come on, Chandra.
-Where are you going?

1520
01:39:54,115 --> 01:39:55,334
-Hey, come with us.
-Go with them.

1521
01:39:55,544 --> 01:39:56,557
Move it, guys!

1522
01:39:56,788 --> 01:39:58,456
Hey, Chunnilal, go ahead,
he'll be back.

1523
01:41:22,988 --> 01:41:24,141
Keep him alive.

1524
01:41:27,616 --> 01:41:29,120
Do only what I ask you to do.

1525
01:41:52,904 --> 01:41:54,643
How long would it take
to go to Poonjolai station?

1526
01:41:54,823 --> 01:41:57,260
Approximately 9 hours, sir.

1527
01:41:57,944 --> 01:41:59,659
-Drive to Poonjolai.
-Okay, Sir.

1528
01:42:02,650 --> 01:42:05,065
Hey, you're the reason
the Police caught him.

1529
01:42:05,623 --> 01:42:06,620
You'll be responsible for his death.

1530
01:42:07,352 --> 01:42:08,651
That's it! They'll kill him for sure.

1531
01:42:09,843 --> 01:42:10,979
Don't show me your face.
Get lost!

1532
01:42:12,137 --> 01:42:13,284
Hey, Karuppu, let's leave.

1533
01:42:14,092 --> 01:42:15,901
Chandra, come with us.

1534
01:42:17,119 --> 01:42:19,057
I won't leave without Das.

1535
01:42:19,563 --> 01:42:20,870
Hey, why are you calling her?

1536
01:42:21,036 --> 01:42:23,635
-Hey, it's Das, damn it.
-So, what do you want me to do?

1537
01:42:24,599 --> 01:42:25,729
It's all done. He's doomed!

1538
01:42:26,044 --> 01:42:27,409
We can't do anything about it.

1539
01:42:29,991 --> 01:42:32,448
If one of you were caught by the Police

1540
01:42:33,340 --> 01:42:35,167
Das wouldn't have abandoned you.

1541
01:42:38,858 --> 01:42:41,479
She's right, Kitty.
We can't leave Das behind.

1542
01:42:41,668 --> 01:42:43,510
Earlier, we left Sebastian behind.
Next, it will be me.

1543
01:42:43,535 --> 01:42:43,818
Hey!

1544
01:42:44,867 --> 01:42:45,526
Bloody fate!

1545
01:42:46,277 --> 01:42:46,737
Let's go!

1546
01:42:49,369 --> 01:42:50,596
What's going on?

1547
01:42:51,269 --> 01:42:52,760
-How could you decide it yourself?
-This guy, I say.

1548
01:42:53,088 --> 01:42:55,221
The car is mine.
And I call the shots.

1549
01:42:55,620 --> 01:42:56,932
My job is to help you cross the border.

1550
01:42:57,007 --> 01:42:58,854
I can't rely on you and get shot in return.

1551
01:43:05,183 --> 01:43:07,503
However, there's a way around it.

1552
01:43:09,659 --> 01:43:10,096
What is it?

1553
01:43:11,672 --> 01:43:12,792
Do you want me?

1554
01:43:13,421 --> 01:43:15,854
Damn, this girl is very open about it.

1555
01:43:19,564 --> 01:43:20,299
First, help us.

1556
01:43:21,545 --> 01:43:22,963
Then I'll do whatever you ask me to.

1557
01:43:26,320 --> 01:43:29,190
Hey, come on!
Let's break him out.

1558
01:43:29,690 --> 01:43:31,971
[in Hindi] Never put off until tomorrow
what you can do today.

1559
01:43:32,248 --> 01:43:34,393
Come on!
Das has helped us a lot.

1560
01:43:34,648 --> 01:43:35,815
Get in the car. Let's go.

1561
01:43:59,458 --> 01:44:01,549
Hey, are you some big gangster?

1562
01:44:02,213 --> 01:44:03,479
Try escaping now.

1563
01:44:04,299 --> 01:44:06,863
I don't understand
why they want to keep you alive.

1564
01:44:10,270 --> 01:44:10,909
Die!

1565
01:44:12,355 --> 01:44:14,963
Hey, acting tough is it?

1566
01:44:16,396 --> 01:44:18,167
Acting tough is it? Is it?

1567
01:44:20,184 --> 01:44:22,838
You're killing the Police.

1568
01:44:23,673 --> 01:44:24,893
And she's killing the Doctor.

1569
01:44:25,284 --> 01:44:27,385
Damn you, people!
Is this a joke to you?

1570
01:44:28,026 --> 01:44:28,932
Come on, tell me!

1571
01:44:35,256 --> 01:44:37,386
Hey, what's her name?

1572
01:44:39,171 --> 01:44:39,884
Hey!

1573
01:44:41,222 --> 01:44:43,141
I'm asking you what her name is.

1574
01:44:47,539 --> 01:44:48,706
What's the name of that Fallen woman?

1575
01:44:58,466 --> 01:45:00,599
Hey, glaring at me, are you?

1576
01:45:01,417 --> 01:45:02,518
So, how does it work?

1577
01:45:03,154 --> 01:45:05,088
Does she make you happy?

1578
01:45:11,107 --> 01:45:12,409
Glaring at me?

1579
01:45:12,821 --> 01:45:14,643
I will ruin her in front of your eyes.

1580
01:45:15,579 --> 01:45:17,534
Hey, constable, bring me a condom.

1581
01:45:27,368 --> 01:45:28,010
Take it out.

1582
01:45:56,231 --> 01:45:57,253
Blast, Kitty!

1583
01:46:11,593 --> 01:46:12,713
Hey, who are you?

1584
01:46:20,493 --> 01:46:23,682
I won't let you die until I'm alive.

1585
01:46:41,232 --> 01:46:42,534
Come on! Come on!

1586
01:46:42,559 --> 01:46:44,307
Chunnilal, bring in the car.

1587
01:47:07,351 --> 01:47:08,510
Hurry up, get in!

1588
01:47:08,779 --> 01:47:09,448
Das?

1589
01:47:12,350 --> 01:47:14,299
-What is it?
-Das!

1590
01:47:15,362 --> 01:47:16,448
Her name is Chandra!

1591
01:47:17,127 --> 01:47:17,776
Not a Fallen woman!

1592
01:47:20,709 --> 01:47:22,088
Das, get out of there.

1593
01:47:22,653 --> 01:47:24,693
-Hey, drive away.
-Come on, Das!

1594
01:47:26,093 --> 01:47:26,971
Go! Go! Go!

1595
01:47:39,761 --> 01:47:44,120
"Eyes, don't fade away"

1596
01:47:44,488 --> 01:47:46,854
"The solace of your shadow... "

1597
01:47:52,043 --> 01:47:56,495
"Let the silence linger"

1598
01:47:56,818 --> 01:47:59,346
"As if I were your breath... "

1599
01:48:19,101 --> 01:48:19,909
-Bhojraj!
-Yes, Sir.

1600
01:48:20,242 --> 01:48:22,987
Despite the shoot-at-sight order,
why did you hold it?

1601
01:48:23,860 --> 01:48:24,784
You let him slip away again.

1602
01:48:25,176 --> 01:48:27,643
Because of you,
the station's inspector is dead.

1603
01:48:28,394 --> 01:48:29,737
Four other officers
are admitted to the hospital.

1604
01:48:30,444 --> 01:48:32,799
Bhojraj,
I'll give you 24 hours.

1605
01:48:33,348 --> 01:48:36,042
Das, his team,
and the new girl along with them...

1606
01:48:36,401 --> 01:48:37,557
kill them all.

1607
01:48:37,956 --> 01:48:40,042
He must not cross the border to Andhra.

1608
01:48:44,203 --> 01:48:45,870
Okay, Sir, I'll finish them all.

1609
01:48:46,918 --> 01:48:48,003
To hell with you!

1610
01:48:53,041 --> 01:48:54,838
Is surveillance still on Das's father?

1611
01:48:55,195 --> 01:48:56,690
Yes, Sir, we're on it.

1612
01:48:58,375 --> 01:48:59,854
-Manoj, Rajarishi.
-Sir!

1613
01:48:59,879 --> 01:49:02,341
You two take the local team's
support and trace in Erode.

1614
01:49:02,366 --> 01:49:02,831
Sure, Sir.

1615
01:49:03,364 --> 01:49:04,862
Ashraf and I are going to Vellore.

1616
01:49:06,396 --> 01:49:08,768
-I reckon he will come to meet his father.
-Yes, Sir.

1617
01:49:11,974 --> 01:49:13,647
Isn't family a weakness, Ashraf?

1618
01:49:15,160 --> 01:49:15,876
Let's go!

1619
01:49:28,527 --> 01:49:30,503
Hey, check if you could find a rod.

1620
01:49:39,297 --> 01:49:39,659
Wait!

1621
01:49:43,464 --> 01:49:45,284
Listen, he does not like you.

1622
01:49:46,251 --> 01:49:47,034
It's better if you leave.

1623
01:49:51,302 --> 01:49:52,104
I don't understand what's happening.

1624
01:49:53,789 --> 01:49:54,628
I'm feeling heavy.

1625
01:49:57,343 --> 01:49:59,299
She's an amazing girl.
Golden-hearted.

1626
01:50:02,626 --> 01:50:03,612
That's why I'm scared.

1627
01:50:08,513 --> 01:50:09,540
I lost many loved ones.

1628
01:50:10,166 --> 01:50:12,924
Hey, Das,
why are you thinking about the past?

1629
01:50:14,114 --> 01:50:16,010
She's considering you as her world.

1630
01:50:17,289 --> 01:50:18,792
In the morning, after you got caught...

1631
01:50:21,795 --> 01:50:23,065
Kitty wanted to leave right away.

1632
01:50:23,729 --> 01:50:27,526
But she stood her ground
and refused to leave without you.

1633
01:50:30,137 --> 01:50:31,034
I'll give you money.
Leave!

1634
01:50:33,283 --> 01:50:34,143
That's good for everyone.

1635
01:50:44,444 --> 01:50:46,612
That cheapo... Chunnilal.

1636
01:50:47,934 --> 01:50:48,846
He, too, wanted to leave.

1637
01:50:50,250 --> 01:50:53,354
But she somehow convinced him to help us.

1638
01:50:55,144 --> 01:50:56,088
She's a good girl.

1639
01:50:56,389 --> 01:50:57,620
Of course, she's a good girl.

1640
01:50:58,303 --> 01:50:59,292
How did she convince him?

1641
01:50:59,745 --> 01:51:00,838
Why don't you tell him everything?

1642
01:51:10,449 --> 01:51:12,534
Bear this in mind.
That girl will be the death of us.

1643
01:51:13,158 --> 01:51:13,987
I'm warning you guys.

1644
01:51:15,556 --> 01:51:17,151
Hey, how did she convince him?

1645
01:51:18,639 --> 01:51:20,573
You see... You see...

1646
01:51:23,354 --> 01:51:25,104
They don't know how to treat a woman.

1647
01:51:25,488 --> 01:51:26,385
Bloody hooligans!

1648
01:51:27,170 --> 01:51:29,010
That's why listen to me
and let go of them.

1649
01:51:30,311 --> 01:51:33,148
Anyhow, the Police will kill them all.

1650
01:51:34,874 --> 01:51:36,995
You cannot keep saving them like a hero.

1651
01:51:37,652 --> 01:51:39,652
They're not going to help you
cross the border.

1652
01:51:39,950 --> 01:51:41,292
I'm responsible for their safety.

1653
01:51:45,162 --> 01:51:45,867
Chandra...

1654
01:51:46,826 --> 01:51:47,812
Think about it.

1655
01:51:48,530 --> 01:51:49,922
You get involved with 10 men in a day.

1656
01:51:50,906 --> 01:51:52,945
But you haven't done it
for the past couple of days.

1657
01:51:53,710 --> 01:51:54,789
That's why you're upset.

1658
01:51:55,758 --> 01:51:58,226
Forget about everything.
We'll have fun.

1659
01:51:58,857 --> 01:52:00,211
We can have a lot of fun.

1660
01:52:01,171 --> 01:52:03,141
I have an elite list of clients.

1661
01:52:03,324 --> 01:52:05,122
We can earn in millions, Chandra.

1662
01:52:07,354 --> 01:52:09,023
Also, our deal is pending.

1663
01:52:10,527 --> 01:52:12,320
They will sleep in a while.

1664
01:52:13,422 --> 01:52:14,195
Just 10 minutes.

1665
01:52:18,342 --> 01:52:20,508
I'm enraged. Go away.

1666
01:52:21,822 --> 01:52:24,414
I'm freaking desperate.
I won't go.

1667
01:52:24,850 --> 01:52:26,094
You should leave.

1668
01:52:28,046 --> 01:52:28,828
Damn you, woman.

1669
01:52:29,460 --> 01:52:31,523
Once the work is done,
you're going back on your word.

1670
01:52:32,370 --> 01:52:34,672
Just because you wore a new saree...

1671
01:52:35,542 --> 01:52:36,445
won't make you a virtuous woman.

1672
01:52:37,833 --> 01:52:38,726
You're a Fallen woman!

1673
01:52:46,275 --> 01:52:47,000
Yes, Das!

1674
01:52:51,606 --> 01:52:53,484
As he helped you escape...

1675
01:52:53,976 --> 01:52:54,859
he wants me.

1676
01:52:55,263 --> 01:52:57,523
When I questioned?
He's calling me a Fallen woman.

1677
01:52:58,090 --> 01:53:00,703
Oh, no, Das! I did not say it.

1678
01:53:01,365 --> 01:53:02,851
I did not say anything like that.

1679
01:53:06,247 --> 01:53:08,086
Das, I did not say it.

1680
01:53:08,776 --> 01:53:10,356
In fact, I called her an angel.

1681
01:53:10,388 --> 01:53:13,101
But I think she misheard it.

1682
01:53:13,768 --> 01:53:15,922
Das, why would I do something like that?

1683
01:53:18,195 --> 01:53:20,117
Das! Das!

1684
01:53:21,143 --> 01:53:23,891
Either smoke it or put it back inside.

1685
01:53:24,770 --> 01:53:26,391
You've been tapping for a while now.

1686
01:53:31,109 --> 01:53:33,132
Do you know why I splattered
the Police officer's brain?

1687
01:53:52,591 --> 01:53:56,328
Except for you, everyone else
sees me in the wrong way.

1688
01:54:04,222 --> 01:54:06,203
Other than my name
what do you know about me?

1689
01:54:08,051 --> 01:54:09,562
For the past two days,
only you've been talking.

1690
01:54:11,210 --> 01:54:13,078
I know everything about you.

1691
01:54:15,106 --> 01:54:16,945
When you were young,
you lost your mother.

1692
01:54:17,768 --> 01:54:20,008
Your father does not talk to you.

1693
01:54:20,353 --> 01:54:23,539
You lost your friend Sebastian.

1694
01:54:24,411 --> 01:54:26,414
Parvathy's death in Madras.

1695
01:54:27,496 --> 01:54:30,875
You're afraid I, too, might die.

1696
01:54:32,324 --> 01:54:33,187
I know a lot, though.

1697
01:54:34,961 --> 01:54:40,055
Beyond everything, are you contemplating
because of what I was before?

1698
01:54:42,548 --> 01:54:44,601
That's one thing I don't know about you.

1699
01:54:45,211 --> 01:54:46,211
Don't talk nonsense.

1700
01:54:47,120 --> 01:54:48,206
That's not what I am thinking about.

1701
01:54:51,508 --> 01:54:52,742
So, it's the fear.

1702
01:54:57,732 --> 01:54:59,328
When the Police caught you...

1703
01:54:59,969 --> 01:55:02,317
I was scared I might not see you again.

1704
01:55:03,655 --> 01:55:09,445
As Kitty suggests, let's drop everything,
go far away, and live a reformed life.

1705
01:55:11,799 --> 01:55:14,500
I wish to live my life with you, Das.

1706
01:55:34,980 --> 01:55:36,797
Hey, let's quit everything.

1707
01:55:37,675 --> 01:55:38,437
We'll find another job.

1708
01:55:39,318 --> 01:55:40,789
We'll think about killing Bhojraj.

1709
01:55:54,015 --> 01:55:56,281
All sounds good. Let's go.

1710
01:55:57,430 --> 01:55:58,031
But not with her.

1711
01:55:59,406 --> 01:56:00,633
I don't get it.
What do you mean?

1712
01:56:10,145 --> 01:56:12,101
Leave her here.
Let's not bring her along.

1713
01:56:15,123 --> 01:56:16,211
I'm not coming without her.

1714
01:56:23,097 --> 01:56:24,535
You don't have to come.
We are leaving.

1715
01:56:24,561 --> 01:56:25,960
-Hey, Kitty!
-Shut up, damn it!

1716
01:56:26,013 --> 01:56:27,047
Don't test my patience

1717
01:56:34,329 --> 01:56:35,359
Already, a girl died because of you.

1718
01:56:35,715 --> 01:56:36,750
Yet you want to bring her along.

1719
01:56:37,391 --> 01:56:38,401
-Kitty!
-I don't wish to die because of her.

1720
01:56:39,734 --> 01:56:40,745
I'm not ready for it.

1721
01:56:40,989 --> 01:56:42,846
You may stick together.
We're going our way.

1722
01:56:44,469 --> 01:56:46,065
Why are you glaring at me?
Why?

1723
01:56:46,555 --> 01:56:47,128
Hey!

1724
01:56:50,463 --> 01:56:52,566
It's not only your life,
but also our lives are at stake.

1725
01:56:52,614 --> 01:56:54,174
-Why are you speaking indifferently?
-Shut up, damn it!

1726
01:56:54,400 --> 01:56:57,073
-Don't speak like a crazy person.
-He won't leave her behind.

1727
01:56:57,214 --> 01:56:58,268
He's panicking
if something happens to her.

1728
01:56:58,562 --> 01:56:59,307
Hey!

1729
01:57:04,139 --> 01:57:05,878
Listen, I'm saying it.
She's a Fallen woman!

1730
01:57:06,013 --> 01:57:06,697
Try denying it!

1731
01:57:06,722 --> 01:57:08,057
-Hey, don't speak ill about a woman.
-Kitty, don't!

1732
01:57:08,082 --> 01:57:08,846
Take your hands off me.

1733
01:57:09,299 --> 01:57:11,112
I'm saying it to your face.
She's a Fallen woman!

1734
01:57:11,216 --> 01:57:12,424
-How are you?
-Das, calm down!

1735
01:57:12,684 --> 01:57:14,057
What else do you expect me to say?

1736
01:57:30,033 --> 01:57:32,174
Hey! Hey, what are you doing?

1737
01:57:32,497 --> 01:57:33,285
What are you doing?

1738
01:57:33,310 --> 01:57:35,307
Hey, shut up. Stop screaming.

1739
01:57:35,373 --> 01:57:36,642
-Das!
-Hereafter, I'm everything to you.

1740
01:57:36,673 --> 01:57:38,190
-Stop the car!
-I'll take care of you.

1741
01:57:46,196 --> 01:57:48,120
Karuppu! Karuppu!

1742
01:57:56,165 --> 01:57:58,049
-Hey, stop the car!
-They won't make it out alive.

1743
01:57:58,074 --> 01:57:59,120
-Stop!
-I won't stop the car.

1744
01:57:59,145 --> 01:58:00,402
Hey, crazy woman.

1745
01:58:03,912 --> 01:58:05,138
Don't you hear me, woman?

1746
01:58:06,488 --> 01:58:07,544
How dare you?

1747
01:58:11,612 --> 01:58:12,366
Chandra!

1748
01:58:18,686 --> 01:58:21,792
Why don't you agree to get out
of here and earn more money?

1749
01:58:22,293 --> 01:58:23,646
Enough with your theatrics!

1750
01:58:24,220 --> 01:58:26,661
Das is sweet in your eyes,
but I'm bitter, right?

1751
01:58:58,716 --> 01:59:00,045
Freaking Chunnilal!

1752
01:59:35,752 --> 01:59:36,271
Das!

1753
01:59:39,523 --> 01:59:40,247
Das!

1754
01:59:45,377 --> 01:59:46,185
Kitty, hear me out.

1755
01:59:47,134 --> 01:59:49,100
-Wait! Wait!
-Let go of me.

1756
01:59:49,140 --> 01:59:50,450
We need him alive.

1757
01:59:51,286 --> 01:59:53,497
Please hear me out.
We need him alive.

1758
01:59:54,142 --> 01:59:54,844
Let go of me!

1759
02:00:02,389 --> 02:00:03,607
Karuppu!

1760
02:00:03,658 --> 02:00:04,747
-Das!
-Karuppu!

1761
02:00:07,214 --> 02:00:07,755
Das!

1762
02:00:13,833 --> 02:00:15,891
Okay, Sir. Sure, Sir.

1763
02:00:26,619 --> 02:00:28,601
Why are you being so egoistic
with your son?

1764
02:00:29,408 --> 02:00:30,421
I, too, have a son.

1765
02:00:31,109 --> 02:00:33,172
He was dancing to his wife's tunes.

1766
02:00:35,008 --> 02:00:36,609
Lately, all sons have become the same.

1767
02:00:37,176 --> 02:00:40,984
I fulfilled every responsibility
I could as a father.

1768
02:00:41,662 --> 02:00:44,476
His one mistake ruined everything.

1769
02:00:45,319 --> 02:00:47,062
I'm enraged, you know.

1770
02:00:47,894 --> 02:00:50,332
I'm not going to cross the border
until I kill them all.

1771
02:00:50,960 --> 02:00:53,203
Kitty, you better leave.

1772
02:00:54,004 --> 02:00:55,320
Try to live a good life.

1773
02:01:01,351 --> 02:01:03,258
After this, a reformed life
doesn't make sense to me.

1774
02:01:05,425 --> 02:01:07,141
I won't leave
until I have killed everyone.

1775
02:01:08,510 --> 02:01:09,633
Even if it costs my life.

1776
02:01:10,670 --> 02:01:13,234
To avoid sharing wealth
with their sister...

1777
02:01:13,586 --> 02:01:17,008
my brother-in-laws tried to
betray my wife.

1778
02:01:18,153 --> 02:01:20,367
But my wife is a headstrong woman.
She didn't let it go.

1779
02:01:20,776 --> 02:01:23,516
She threatened to go to court.

1780
02:01:24,435 --> 02:01:25,617
Do you know what they did?

1781
02:01:26,092 --> 02:01:30,906
They hacked down their sister
and brutally killed her.

1782
02:01:32,162 --> 02:01:33,539
I was enraged.

1783
02:01:34,402 --> 02:01:37,336
Don't I know how to pick up the sickle
and kill them all?

1784
02:01:37,756 --> 02:01:39,383
But I did not do it.
Do you know why?

1785
02:01:39,969 --> 02:01:42,586
Because my son was 13-14 years old.

1786
02:01:43,878 --> 02:01:45,531
I suppressed my anger...

1787
02:01:45,803 --> 02:01:47,828
borrowed money
and provided him with education.

1788
02:01:48,521 --> 02:01:49,359
Why?

1789
02:01:49,836 --> 02:01:53,411
If he studies well,
he'll help me in the future.

1790
02:01:53,888 --> 02:01:54,750
Did he come through?

1791
02:01:57,060 --> 02:02:01,570
He was determined to avenge his
mother's death and killed his uncles.

1792
02:02:02,563 --> 02:02:04,516
Why the heck
should I still provide him education?

1793
02:02:06,164 --> 02:02:07,922
You have decided to kill them.

1794
02:02:09,121 --> 02:02:12,219
But before, deliver the money
where it belongs.

1795
02:02:14,558 --> 02:02:16,228
Also, meet your father.

1796
02:02:18,187 --> 02:02:19,844
I agree,
you have every right to be angry.

1797
02:02:20,809 --> 02:02:22,203
But this is too much ego!

1798
02:02:23,345 --> 02:02:24,898
Pick up the phone and speak to him.

1799
02:02:25,623 --> 02:02:27,414
He called you
because he's long to speak to you.

1800
02:02:31,704 --> 02:02:33,445
The Police will be watching my father.

1801
02:02:45,938 --> 02:02:47,586
Let him mind his business.

1802
02:02:48,611 --> 02:02:51,125
No good can come of talking to him.

1803
02:02:51,608 --> 02:02:53,930
I'm more egoistic than you are.

1804
02:02:54,433 --> 02:02:56,484
Because he spoke against me...

1805
02:02:57,001 --> 02:02:58,741
I stopped seeing him for good.

1806
02:03:00,538 --> 02:03:03,719
Yet you're advising me.

1807
02:03:04,466 --> 02:03:06,164
Where is your son now?

1808
02:03:07,133 --> 02:03:07,711
Hello.

1809
02:03:09,172 --> 02:03:09,953
Yes, Son.

1810
02:03:11,256 --> 02:03:14,781
After getting married,
he had a child and lived a good life.

1811
02:03:15,822 --> 02:03:20,063
Later, he didn't want to do
anything with me or my wealth.

1812
02:03:20,728 --> 02:03:21,249
Pride!

1813
02:03:23,258 --> 02:03:25,250
In the end,
he sold his agricultural land

1814
02:03:26,019 --> 02:03:27,961
but I got a news
that he never returned with the money.

1815
02:03:29,936 --> 02:03:33,359
My daughter-in-law is sure he stopped
at the checkpost to help the police.

1816
02:03:34,025 --> 02:03:34,898
I did question the Police.

1817
02:03:35,148 --> 02:03:37,078
They said, "He'll return home
once he runs out of money."

1818
02:03:37,414 --> 02:03:38,492
And branded him a drunkard!

1819
02:03:40,466 --> 02:03:41,914
They didn't even file
a missing person case.

1820
02:03:43,311 --> 02:03:45,922
We consulted many lawyers
and police, but in vain.

1821
02:03:46,105 --> 02:03:47,861
Get out of here.
I'm warning you!

1822
02:03:48,117 --> 02:03:50,181
If you don't leave,
I'll book you under a brothel case.

1823
02:03:50,275 --> 02:03:53,311
If the police behave like this,
who do we go to for help?

1824
02:03:53,529 --> 02:03:55,266
-Hey, get out of her.
-Oh, no!

1825
02:03:55,544 --> 02:03:57,766
Get out!
Take them away from here.

1826
02:03:58,326 --> 02:04:02,351
I was suffering in pain without knowing
if he was alive or dead.

1827
02:04:07,652 --> 02:04:10,508
But the anger festering inside me
refused to spare them.

1828
02:04:11,984 --> 02:04:13,945
That's when I went to your son,
explained everything,

1829
02:04:13,970 --> 02:04:15,359
and identified them.

1830
02:04:24,119 --> 02:04:24,984
Are you saying

1831
02:04:26,345 --> 02:04:27,273
that you know my son?

1832
02:04:28,679 --> 02:04:30,617
I know your son better than you.

1833
02:04:31,782 --> 02:04:33,726
When a crime is committed,
the police step in to solve it.

1834
02:04:34,017 --> 02:04:36,828
But when the police themselves commit
a crime, who'd step in to question it?

1835
02:04:41,141 --> 02:04:41,781
Sir!

1836
02:04:43,083 --> 02:04:46,516
They're hiding out
in an old paper mill near a quarry.

1837
02:04:47,356 --> 02:04:50,164
We have surrounded them.
Get here soon, Sir.

1838
02:04:51,290 --> 02:04:51,664
Okay!

1839
02:04:53,295 --> 02:04:54,750
Ashraf, quickly start the car.

1840
02:04:54,790 --> 02:04:56,922
Alert the entire team.
They're at the old paper mill.

1841
02:04:57,686 --> 02:04:58,859
Hurry up! Hurry up!

1842
02:04:59,244 --> 02:05:00,055
I need backup.

1843
02:05:00,080 --> 02:05:01,930
They only listen to affluent people.

1844
02:05:02,531 --> 02:05:04,023
They don't even consider us
as human beings.

1845
02:05:06,443 --> 02:05:08,328
But if you treat them as they deserve
and question they'll listen.

1846
02:05:08,851 --> 02:05:09,881
Your son questioned them!

1847
02:05:14,094 --> 02:05:14,734
Hey!

1848
02:05:17,073 --> 02:05:17,880
Come on!

1849
02:05:18,447 --> 02:05:20,180
Hello, inform the local station.

1850
02:05:20,748 --> 02:05:22,164
Come on, get in the car.

1851
02:05:28,940 --> 02:05:31,617
They killed my son
and threw him in the bushes.

1852
02:05:33,459 --> 02:05:36,167
In the end,
I saw only my son's corpse.

1853
02:05:44,490 --> 02:05:45,531
Go! Go! Go!

1854
02:05:46,776 --> 02:05:49,799
Did you say you struggled to
provide an education for your son?

1855
02:05:51,403 --> 02:05:56,252
My son, too, sold all his wealth
to support his son's education.

1856
02:05:57,035 --> 02:05:57,822
We lost that money as well.

1857
02:05:59,377 --> 02:06:00,111
False pride!

1858
02:06:01,385 --> 02:06:04,041
I'm a father.
Why should I let go of my ego?

1859
02:06:05,438 --> 02:06:06,627
I held on to it.

1860
02:06:10,822 --> 02:06:12,540
Now I feel like talking to my son.

1861
02:06:13,649 --> 02:06:15,713
But my son is no more to talk to.

1862
02:06:30,411 --> 02:06:31,783
Sir, please come.

1863
02:06:32,001 --> 02:06:32,408
Sure, Son.

1864
02:06:36,355 --> 02:06:37,518
You keep the motor to yourself.

1865
02:06:40,751 --> 02:06:42,588
Your son is here. Talk to him.

1866
02:07:02,254 --> 02:07:04,357
-I brought a bag.
-It's okay. You can keep it.

1867
02:07:10,544 --> 02:07:11,232
Study well!

1868
02:07:13,805 --> 02:07:14,997
-Go safe.
-Bye, Son.

1869
02:07:36,119 --> 02:07:38,107
I called you many times.
You didn't answer.

1870
02:07:39,148 --> 02:07:40,454
Dad, are you never going to
talk to me again?

1871
02:07:44,965 --> 02:07:46,490
Why should I even talk to you?

1872
02:07:48,215 --> 02:07:49,735
I warned you enough.

1873
02:07:50,347 --> 02:07:52,700
But you didn't pay heed to me
and ruined everything.

1874
02:07:54,202 --> 02:07:56,841
-What's left to talk about anymore?
-You should've spoken, Dad.

1875
02:07:57,451 --> 02:07:58,404
You should've spoken!

1876
02:07:58,962 --> 02:08:00,365
You should've knocked
some sense into me with it.

1877
02:08:00,958 --> 02:08:04,068
Who knows!
I may have listened to you.

1878
02:08:22,936 --> 02:08:25,950
Girl! Who are you?

1879
02:08:26,857 --> 02:08:28,224
How could you trust him?

1880
02:08:28,485 --> 02:08:31,404
I'm his father.
Look at my condition.

1881
02:08:32,891 --> 02:08:34,975
Please be smart
and take care of your life.

1882
02:08:44,708 --> 02:08:46,994
You think you're off the radar.

1883
02:08:47,220 --> 02:08:48,661
The Police have tracked you down.

1884
02:08:48,804 --> 02:08:50,412
First, find a way to vacate this shop.

1885
02:08:53,470 --> 02:08:54,601
I know how to take care of myself.

1886
02:08:55,090 --> 02:08:57,883
Do what you came for
and be on your way.

1887
02:08:58,670 --> 02:09:04,343
"I break away... "

1888
02:09:06,719 --> 02:09:08,891
"I don’t obey"

1889
02:09:09,322 --> 02:09:10,908
Bomb!

1890
02:09:14,705 --> 02:09:19,943
"I break away... "

1891
02:09:22,733 --> 02:09:24,927
"I don’t obey"

1892
02:09:25,163 --> 02:09:26,990
I don't know why.
But I wanted to see you one last time.

1893
02:09:27,433 --> 02:09:29,712
Not sure
If I were to get another chance.

1894
02:09:30,471 --> 02:09:31,455
So, are you done?

1895
02:09:35,756 --> 02:09:37,746
If I escape from the Police and return

1896
02:09:38,192 --> 02:09:39,723
let's try to live as father and son.

1897
02:09:39,758 --> 02:09:41,740
Fine, we'll try to make it happen.

1898
02:09:46,950 --> 02:09:52,115
"I break away..."

1899
02:09:54,963 --> 02:09:57,187
"I don’t obey"

1900
02:10:02,706 --> 02:10:08,232
"I break away..."

1901
02:10:10,699 --> 02:10:12,699
"I don’t obey"

1902
02:10:12,724 --> 02:10:13,583
Das, make it fast!

1903
02:10:18,927 --> 02:10:24,300
"I break away..."

1904
02:10:34,082 --> 02:10:34,706
Hey!

1905
02:10:35,511 --> 02:10:36,453
He's on top!

1906
02:13:15,975 --> 02:13:16,987
You check upstairs!

1907
02:13:24,366 --> 02:13:25,174
Hey, Kitty!

1908
02:13:33,793 --> 02:13:34,698
Did you take a bullet?

1909
02:13:36,616 --> 02:13:38,823
Even when I'm about to die
you're late.

1910
02:13:41,807 --> 02:13:42,869
I thought you guys wouldn't come.

1911
02:13:43,401 --> 02:13:44,542
How could I not come for you?

1912
02:14:07,361 --> 02:14:08,260
Hey!

1913
02:14:29,942 --> 02:14:31,932
I won't rest until I kill you,
damn it!

1914
02:15:29,456 --> 02:15:29,917
Dad!

1915
02:15:30,354 --> 02:15:32,276
-Ameena! Ameena!
-What happened, Dad?

1916
02:15:32,422 --> 02:15:34,409
-How are you, dear?
-Why do you sound weird?

1917
02:15:34,434 --> 02:15:35,645
-Did you eat?
-Dad, where are you?

1918
02:15:36,096 --> 02:15:37,023
How is your mother?

1919
02:15:55,826 --> 02:15:57,273
Dad, when will you come home?

1920
02:15:57,988 --> 02:15:58,922
Dad!

1921
02:15:59,130 --> 02:16:00,729
-Dad, what happened?
-I'll come soon.

1922
02:16:00,754 --> 02:16:01,516
Dad!

1923
02:16:02,764 --> 02:16:03,750
I'll be home soon.

1924
02:16:18,804 --> 02:16:21,320
Dad! What happened, Dad?

1925
02:16:21,345 --> 02:16:22,331
Dad, can you hear me?

1926
02:16:26,108 --> 02:16:27,870
Dad, what's that sound?

1927
02:16:27,895 --> 02:16:29,159
Dad, can you hear me?

1928
02:16:29,933 --> 02:16:31,432
Dad, what's that sound?

1929
02:16:31,625 --> 02:16:32,768
Dad, say something.

1930
02:16:32,793 --> 02:16:34,018
Can you hear me?

1931
02:16:34,422 --> 02:16:36,568
Dad! Dad, what's happening?

1932
02:16:37,294 --> 02:16:38,075
Dad!

1933
02:16:38,505 --> 02:16:39,990
Dad, say something.

1934
02:16:40,023 --> 02:16:42,505
Dad, can you hear me?

1935
02:16:42,913 --> 02:16:44,990
Dad, what happened?

1936
02:16:45,511 --> 02:16:47,083
When will you return home?

1937
02:16:47,108 --> 02:16:48,599
Dad! Dad!

1938
02:16:49,397 --> 02:16:51,169
Dad, can you hear me?

1939
02:16:51,568 --> 02:16:53,801
Dad, can you hear me?

1940
02:16:54,089 --> 02:16:55,443
Dad, say something.

1941
02:16:57,946 --> 02:16:58,575
Dad...

1942
02:17:01,258 --> 02:17:02,892
Dad, please say something.

1943
02:17:02,923 --> 02:17:05,076
I'm very scared, Dad.

1944
02:17:05,905 --> 02:17:07,177
Dad, say something.

1945
02:17:07,989 --> 02:17:08,706
Dad!

1946
02:17:10,070 --> 02:17:11,393
-Your Dad...
-Uncle!

1947
02:17:12,021 --> 02:17:13,799
and a few policemen are hurt.

1948
02:17:14,187 --> 02:17:16,299
Send an ambulance
to the Vellore paper mill.

1949
02:17:16,324 --> 02:17:17,479
Uncle, who are you?

1950
02:17:18,487 --> 02:17:19,643
What happened to my Dad, Uncle?

1951
02:17:19,813 --> 02:17:21,510
What happened to my Dad--?

1952
02:17:54,918 --> 02:17:56,927
-Kitty, what happened?
-Nothing's wrong.

1953
02:17:58,882 --> 02:18:00,583
Hey, take care of him.

1954
02:18:00,900 --> 02:18:01,434
Hey!

1955
02:18:02,538 --> 02:18:03,615
Where are you planning to go?

1956
02:18:05,904 --> 02:18:07,005
It's a huge world.

1957
02:18:14,774 --> 02:18:15,771
Das!

1958
02:18:20,315 --> 02:18:21,552
As long as she's with you, you're safe.

1959
02:18:38,915 --> 02:18:39,661
Let's go, Kitty!

1960
02:18:43,250 --> 02:18:46,966
We're still listed as rowdies, gangsters,
and extremists in the police files.

1961
02:18:47,869 --> 02:18:49,990
They've written our destiny,
and it cannot be altered.

1962
02:18:50,931 --> 02:18:53,560
But we stopped running
to discover who we truly are.

1963
02:18:54,139 --> 02:18:56,630
With faith that education
will shape Angani's son,

1964
02:18:56,915 --> 02:18:58,794
even this lifeless plastic flower

1965
02:18:59,318 --> 02:19:00,880
and this death-dealing gun,

1966
02:19:01,189 --> 02:19:02,388
as my mother says,

1967
02:19:02,824 --> 02:19:05,458
will send you into this vast world
to build a life.

1968
02:19:17,462 --> 02:19:22,544
www.1TamilMV.meme